# Who reviews what.
#
# The Scorecard's Code-Review check asks for this file to exist, and the file
# earns its place: every change to the crawler, to the security
# configuration, and to the CI surfaces is reviewed by the owner before it
# reaches `main`.
#
# The order matters — the last matching pattern wins — so the specific
# patterns come first and `*` catches the rest.

# The security-sensitive parts: how a request is authenticated and what it
# is allowed to do.
/app/security/          @gazon1
/app/scheduling/        @gazon1
/app/src/main/resources/ @gazon1

# The CI surfaces: a workflow is code that runs with the repository's
# permissions, and it is reviewed like code.
/.github/workflows/      @gazon1
/.github/dependabot.yml  @gazon1
/scripts/ci/            @gazon1
/scripts/check-*.py     @gazon1

# The crawler itself.
/wbparser/              @gazon1

# Everything else.
/*                      @gazon1
